On Thursday 15 September 2005 17:15, Brandon Wirick wrote:
> Question: are {bakrto} and {bakyrto} the same word in any system?

{bakrto} is a variant of {baknrto}, though not considered the same word as 
{bakcange} and {baknycange} are. {bakyrto} is not a word, since any word with 
a consonant cluster and a 'y' is a lujvo, and {rto} is not a rafsi or 
decomposable into rafsi.

